<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862).

  ADS 2 keeps three abstract RecipeDefs, ADS_Cat1 (medieval replacements), ADS_Cat2 (+ simple prosthetics) and
  ADS_Cat3 (+ bionics), each with a hand-curated <recipeUsers> list, and copies those lists onto the real surgery
  recipes in its own last patch. An animal absent from all three lists offers only amputation and euthanasia.
  The lists are cumulative: an animal of Cat3 is in the three.

  The choice follows each animal's vanilla analogue in ADS 2's own list
  (1.6/Defs/AnimalCategories/Animal_Categories.xml, read 2026-10-13):

    - MG_Horse is a horse breed: Horse is in Cat1, Cat2 and Cat3, so all three.
    - MG_TuSun is a Pallas's cat (body size 0.75): Cat and Lynx are in all three, so all three.
    - MG_TiaoShu is a jerboa (body size 0.3) and MG_TuBoShu a marmot (0.6): the small rodents Squirrel, Rat and
      Chinchilla are in Cat1 only (Hare and Raccoon reach Cat2, but are not rodents), so Cat1 only.

  The guard is PatchOperationConditional on ADS_Cat1. Without ADS 2 the xpath selects nothing, no <nomatch> is
  declared, and the operation reports success without logging anything. It is NOT MayRequire: MayRequire on an
  <Operation> is read by nothing, so the operation would apply whether ADS 2 is loaded or not. Every branch of the
  predicate repeats @Name=, since [@Name="A" or "B"] is true for every RecipeDef in the document.

  About.xml declares <loadBefore>SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2</loadBefore>: ADS 2 copies the lists once,
  at its own patch, so this patch has to run first.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[
						@Name="ADS_Cat3" or
						@Name="ADS_Cat2" or
						@Name="ADS_Cat1"
					]/recipeUsers</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>MG_Horse</li>
						<li>MG_TuSun</li>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>MG_TiaoShu</li>
						<li>MG_TuBoShu</li>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
